            "lens": "review-risk",
            "findings": [],
            "evidence": [
              "The change tightens review clearance: exemptions must now bind exactly one commit (base equals the first parent of the head, enforced by Service.oneCommit in both Exempt and the check of stored exemptions), and NewCandidate refuses base==head. Both enforcement points are in the backend (engine/review/app/exempt.go, engine/review/app/check.go, engine/review/review.go), not only in the CLI.",
              "gitexec.Parent invokes git rev-list with an argument vector (no shell) and --end-of-options before the commit, which is already a validated full object name; output is strictly parsed (single line, first token equals the commit, every parent a full object name), so there is no injection or option-smuggling path.",
              "Parent errors fail closed: any git failure refuses the exemption or the head rather than clearing it. No secrets, new dependencies, or data-exposure paths are introduced.",
              "The README note that an edited stored verdict can clear a blocked head is a documentation of pre-existing behavior (check does not compare stored files with role-chain digests), not something this candidate introduced; it is disclosed rather than hidden.",
              "Behavior changes visible to users (bind --base X --head X now exits 1; roles append message naming the exemption) are requested by the change and documented in CHANGELOG and usage text, so they are not unrequested regressions."
            ]
          }
        }
