            "lens": "review-reliability",
            "findings": [],
            "evidence": [
              "Reviewed all 24 changed paths in the patch. The new one-commit rule is enforced in both Service.Exempt (before anything is stored) and exemptedHead in engine/review/app/check.go, which both the single-head check and the chain walk use. A git failure while finding the parent is wrapped and refuses the head. engine/review/app/exempt_test.go covers this for both Exempt and Check.",
              "gitexec.Parent in engine/review/gitexec/gitexec.go validates git's output strictly: the commit must match, the line must be a single one, and every parent must be a full object name. It returns the first parent for a merge and an empty string for a root commit. gitexec_test.go covers the malformed-output cases with a fake runner, and realgit_test.go covers a plain commit, a root commit, a merge and a missing object against real git.",
              "NewCandidate now refuses a range whose base is its head (engine/review/review.go). This is a requested and documented behaviour change, and it is asserted in candidate_test.go and in engine/cmd/review_exempt_range_test.go at the CLI level.",
              "Results are deliberately not held to the one-commit rule, so the correction-round case still clears. TestACleanResultOverTwoCommitsAfterACorrectionRoundStillClears proves that. The regression repro (an exemption stepping over a blocked commit) is proved end to end by TestAnExemptionCannotStepOverAReviewThatBlocksACommitInTheMiddleOfTheChain.",
              "CheckRange gained a stored parameter so the message names the exemption instead of a result. Both call sites pass the right value, and the new test in evidence_test.go asserts both wordings. No reliability gaps found."
            ]
          }
